    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0114" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg107"/>

                <head>No. 64.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatches of May 21 and 28, 1894,
                    have been received. They both relate to the case of Argüello, the murderer of
                    William Wilson, at Rama.</p>
                <p>It will be gratifying to the President to learn that his inst expectations <pb
                        facs="0115" n="108" xml:id="pg108"/> have been fulfilled by the visitation
                    of the condign displeasure of the Nicaraguan Government upon the culpable
                    officials whose connivance frustrated the immediate ends of justice by effecting
                    the culprit’s escape; and it would be additionally satisfactory to be informed
                    that Argüello has been retaken and that the course of law in this singularly
                    aggravated case will be assured.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
